  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It builds a ring of 64 bars as one instanced box node (`instances.box`) with a runtime id, standing on a PBR floor. Typecheck passes, but I couldn't run `vite build` or open the page, so I haven't seen a rendered frame. In particular, the shadow coverage and the exact look are untested.\n\n- **Animation:** each frame, `setInstanceMatrices` rewrites all 64 column-major matrices. Heights come from three travelling sine waves, and each bar faces outward from the ring centre.\n- **Colour:** each bar gets its own colour from an HSL hue gradient around the ring, passed as instance colours on a white base material.\n- **Lighting and camera:** the scene has a neutral environment, a hemisphere light, a shadow-casting directional key light and a bluish fill light. `camera.orbit` with `autoRotate` orbits the camera slowly.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set on the first rendered frame.\n- **Two assumptions I couldn't check:**\n  - I assumed the unit box is centred on its origin, so each bar is lifted by half its height to sit on the floor.\n  - I used `autoRotate` on `camera.orbit` for the orbit. I did not use `app.camera.setPose`, because it may need a feature flag.\n- **Top-level await:** I dropped it (`void app.ready()`), because Vite's default build target may reject it.\n\n",
